## Decision-calendar anchor (what to move, when)

- **Now – Q4 2026:** Board adoption of the standard as a Design Manual amendment before Concourse C/D consultant scoping. This is the last low-cost adoption window.
- **2026–2028:** Standard becomes a required deliverable inside every RFP funded by the ~$5.5B new-debt program; language ties compliance to Grant Assurance 34.
- **FY2028 FAA Reauthorization:** Prepare to update the standard for tightened ACAA and LEP obligations Congress is likely to enact. Do not assume any relaxation.
- **Through Dec 31, 2039:** Standard governs MII conversations by having been adopted upstream of cost-recovery scope, not downstream of it.

## Evidence gaps flagged

- MWAA's existing Design Manual (2020, seven volumes) may already contain acoustic, PA-zoning, STI, or LEQ requirements at some tier. This brief assumes it does not bind at the tier this standard requires; the Strategist should not rely on that assumption without primary confirmation.
- Majority-in-interest thresholds and cost-recovery categorization under the January 1, 2025 Use and Lease Agreement are not verified in primary documents. Airline-economics arguments should be scoped to what the agreement text supports.
- Peer-airport primary documentation for SFO, LCY, HEL, CPH, AMS, DXB, and BCN quiet-airport programs is not in the Stage-0 packet. Any peer quotation used in the final article needs primary confirmation.
